WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.140
This is the Microsoft for Education Daily, for Friday.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.270
Here are the last 24 hours at Microsoft, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.750
Plan ahead. Microsoft's To Do apps retire on June 30, 2027, on every device.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.610
School accounts move to Planner; personal accounts will need another app.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.240
Teaching on Teams? Its new meeting controls are rolling out,

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.870
and you can make them yours.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.870
Pin Record or Raise hand where you want them,

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.870
and Leave sits apart from the rest.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.290
The roadmap now shows Study and Learn assignments rolling out,

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.660
for students 13 plus.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.360
On Windows, Live captions can now caption voices in the room,

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:57.940
as the update rolls out.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.030
For school IT,

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:06.130
shared PCs on hybrid setups can now sign in with no password at all.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.860
Use a passkey on your phone or a security key, on Windows 11 Pro and Enterprise.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.900
Building with AI? Microsoft Foundry's new cost controls,

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.240
in preview, put a budget on a project or agent.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.590
Set it in dollars or tokens, then get an alert,

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.150
or block new requests until it resets.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.220
For group projects,

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:36.960
Planner's colour rules are rolling out: highlight tasks by due date, priority or status.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.960
Buckets get colours too, and task history,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.720
also rolling out, shows what changed and when.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.910
The fine print?

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:51.040
Microsoft says November's Windows hotpatch can stop some apps installing or opening.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.580
There's a registry workaround for now,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.520
and no optional Windows preview update this December.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.570
After hours,

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:06.980
Windows Hello can now brighten your screen to see your face in a dark room.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.580
And the new Windows Search turns on dark m

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.830
ode or Bluetooth straight from the results.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.830
Plus, when something's capturing your screen,

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.320
its border now turns red, not yellow.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.170
Tasks, budgets, updates: whatever next year brings, plan ahead.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Day after day, the updates keep stacking up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.340
Today's board: shipped. Tomorrow's: already building.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
That's one day of updates. Imagine a whole year.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.720
This has been the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?
